---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TextPage from '../components/TextPage.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About — KAVOVO"
  description="Why KAVOVO exists: clear, tested coffee recipes and brewing guides for people making coffee at home."
>
  <TextPage
    eyebrow="About"
    title="Coffee, made clear."
    intro="KAVOVO is a home-coffee handbook: recipes you can follow on a weekday morning, and guides that explain why they work."
  >
    <h2>Why we started</h2>
    <p>
      Most coffee advice sits at one of two extremes. Either it skips the numbers entirely — "add a scoop, pour hot
      water" — or it assumes you already own a refractometer. Neither helps the person standing in the kitchen at 7am
      wondering why today's cup tastes thinner than yesterday's.
    </p>
    <p>
      KAVOVO aims at the middle: exact doses, times and ratios, written plainly, with the reasoning attached. Every
      recipe tells you what to do and what to change when it doesn't taste right.
    </p>

    <h2>How recipes are written</h2>
    <p>Each recipe follows the same rules:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Weights in grams and volumes in millilitres — never "a scoop".</li>
      <li>A starting ratio you can adjust, not a single fixed answer.</li>
      <li>Troubleshooting for the two failures that actually happen: too sour, too bitter.</li>
      <li>Equipment lists that assume a normal kitchen, with alternatives where they exist.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Where a drink depends on technique rather than numbers — milk texture, pour rate — the matching
      <a href="/guides/">brew guide</a> covers it in more detail.
    </p>

    <h2>What's coming</h2>
    <p>
      We're preparing a small range of coffees roasted for specific brew methods, so the beans and the recipe agree with
      each other. You can <a href="/shop/">join the waitlist</a> to hear when it opens.
    </p>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Corrections, questions and disagreements are all welcome — a recipe that fails in your kitchen is useful
      information. Write to us on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </TextPage>
</Layout>
